---
import RepositoryCard from '../components/RepositoryCard.astro';
import repositories from '../data/repositories.json';
import '../styles/site.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer" />
    <meta name="description" content="GitHub Discussions participation, response metrics, and RSS subscriptions." />
    <title>Discussion engagement</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <header class="page-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">GitHub Discussions <span class="prototype">Prototype</span></p>
        <h1>Discussion engagement</h1>
        <p>Follow the conversations. See who participates and which questions get a response.</p>
      </header>

      <section aria-labelledby="leaderboard-heading">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="leaderboard-heading">Repository overview</h2>
          <span class="muted">Live API data · No stored snapshots</span>
        </div>
        {repositories.map((repository) => <RepositoryCard repository={repository} />)}
      </section>

      <section class="access" aria-labelledby="access-heading">
        <div>
          <h2 id="access-heading">Load live metrics</h2>
          <p>GitHub’s GraphQL API requires a token, even for public discussions.</p>
          <p class="muted" id="token-help">Use a fine-grained token with Discussions: read-only access to the enrolled public repositories, or a classic token with no scopes. The token stays in memory, is sent only to api.github.com, and is not saved. Never use a shared or privileged token.</p>
        </div>
        <form id="access-form">
          <label for="github-token">GitHub token</label>
          <input id="github-token" name="token" type="password" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" required aria-describedby="token-help" placeholder="Enter your own read-only token" />
          <div class="form-actions">
            <button type="submit">Read live metrics</button>
            <button type="button" class="secondary" id="cancel" hidden>Cancel</button>
          </div>
          <p class="muted">A complete fetch includes older discussions to distinguish new and returning participants. Large threads may take several requests.</p>
        </form>
        <noscript><p>JavaScript is required for live metrics. RSS subscriptions work without it.</p></noscript>
      </section>

      <details class="methodology">
        <summary>What these metrics measure</summary>
        <p>Counts cover the trailing 30 days, ending when the fetch starts. Comments include nested replies and activity on older discussions. Participants include identifiable users and bots; deleted authors cannot be counted as distinct people.</p>
        <p>Q&A means any category that accepts answers. Answer status is current, not historical. First response excludes the discussion author’s own responses and discussions with no identifiable outside response.</p>
        <p>New participants have no earlier visible contribution in this repository’s discussions. Returning participants do. Deleted contributions and category moves limit historical accuracy.</p>
        <p>Partial fetches show no data for affected metrics, not partial counts. The sparkline and trend are unavailable: this prototype does not store the snapshots needed for those comparisons.</p>
      </details>
    </main>
    <script>
      import '../scripts/dashboard';
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
